        <body>
            <div xml:id="d624">

                <pb facs="1045" n="949" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg949"/>

                <head>No. 622.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 18, 1873</date>.
                        (Received December 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 844.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith a copy
                    and a translation of a note received to-day from the minister of state, in reply
                    to mine of the 16th instant, in which I invited his attention to the reports
                    published in the Havana papers of the 14th, from which it appears that more of
                    the persons captured on board the Virginius had been shot, leaving only some
                    eighteen survivors of the whole number taken. These statements receive, as you
                    will observe, a vague denial, which is weakened by the consideration that such
                    reports, in relation to a matter so conspicuous and of so much importance, if
                    erroneous, could not have escaped the very rigid censorship of the press at
                    Havana.</p>
                <p>The remainder of the note seems to be an amplification of the minister’s <pb
                        facs="1046" n="950" xml:id="pg950"/> reply to our demand for reparation, in
                    which he assumes that the Government of the United States is as ignorant of the
                    facts of the case as his excellency professes himself to be.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>D. E. SICKLES.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d624-a1.xml" xpointer="d624-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
